KW  - Nested named entity recognition
KW  - Relation-aware
KW  - Span diffusion
KW  - Self-conditioning mechanism
AB  - Nested named entity recognition (NER) requires accurate identification of overlapping entity boundaries when entities share tokens. To address this challenge, we propose SpanDiff, a relation-aware span diffusion framework that formulates structured prediction as a diffusion process over candidate span sets in a continuous latent space. SpanDiff maps discrete boundary indices into bounded continuous intervals through linear projection, enabling differentiable optimization. During reverse denoising, a relation-aware Transformer decoder incorporates positional inductive biases based on Intersection over Union and center distance to model dependencies among candidate spans. A self-conditioning mechanism further leverages predictions from previous denoising steps as dynamic priors to guide boundary refinement. We evaluate SpanDiff on four nested NER benchmarks, including ACE2004, ACE2005, GENIA, and KBP2017, and two flat NER benchmarks, CoNLL2003 and OntoNotes. Experimental results show that SpanDiff achieves strong performance on nested NER benchmarks and competitive results on flat NER benchmarks. The open-source code is publicly available at https://github.com/yqx35/spandiff.
