AB  - In recent years, coverless image steganography has gained prominence as a crucial and rapidly evolving research focus within the broader domain of image steganography. Different from traditional image steganography, it can achieve information hiding without modifying the cover image. With the development of diffusion model, this technique is also applied in coverless image steganography. This review presents a systematic synthesis, consolidating the key advancements achieved to date and identifying the fundamental challenges still impeding progress in coverless image steganography research employing diffusion models. Firstly, this paper introduces the basic principles of coverless image steganography and clearly categorizes the coverless image steganography system, dividing the coverless image steganography methods into two approaches: mapping-based and generation-based. It then details the developmental history and representative methods of these two approaches, along with their respective advantages and disadvantages, before introducing the latest application of diffusion models within this field. Based on the different objects to be hidden, coverless image steganography based on diffusion models is also divided into two types: image-to-image and text-to-image, and the representative methods of the two types are summarized in detail. To facilitate readers’ understanding of the advantages and disadvantages of these methods, we have summarized the evaluation metrics and experimental methods that may be used in the experiments, and analyzed the experimental results based on the summarized experimental evaluation system. This review comprehensively outlines coverless image steganography, covering its basic principles, research progress, experimental results, and challenges faced.
