KW  - Nd-Fe-B magnets
KW  - Grain boundary diffusion
KW  - Coercivity
KW  - Service performance
AB  - The rapid development of the motors for new energy vehicles puts high requirements on the coercivity and thermal stability of rare earth (RE) permanent magnets. Grain boundary diffusion (GBD) technology using heavy rare earth (HRE)-based alloys or compounds as the diffusion sources has been demonstrated as an effective approach for enhancing the coercivity of sintered Nd-Fe-B-based magnet with minimum loss of remanence. Although HREs have been greatly reduced in the GBD-treated magnets, they still account for the significant material cost of high-performance Nd-Fe-B magnets. Further reducing the content of HRE in the magnets is still the expectation from industry. Recently, HRE elements have been alloyed with other elements in the diffusion sources for achieving not only high coercivity enhancement but also lowered materials cost. On the other hand, the grain boundary modification by GBD has critical effects on the service performance of Nd-Fe-B magnets, such as corrosion resistance, mechanical properties, and electrical conductivity. This review describes the recent research progress in the GBD of Nd-Fe-B magnets. Firstly, modifying the composition of the HRE-based diffusion sources by alloying with non-HRE elements to enhance diffusion efficiency and performance/cost ratio has been summarized. The roles of the light RE (LRE), high abundance RE (ARE) and other RE (ORE) elements of Nd, Pr, La, Ce, Y, Gd and Ho have been analyzed. Secondly, the effects of GBD by various diffusion sources on the service performance of Nd-Fe-B magnets are also discussed. In particular, the influences of RE and non-RE element distributions in the diffused magnets on the physical, chemical, and mechanical properties of the magnets have been clarified. Finally, the challenges and potential advancements in the GBD technology and diffusion source have been reviewed and proposed, respectively, regarding the development of high-performance and cost-effective magnets for industrial applications.
