AB  - The subsequent space grouting filling technology aims to safely, greenly and efficiently treat coal-based solid waste (CSW). In view of the four-in-one system problem of grouting material-slurry transportation-filling space-rock stratum control in the process of diffusion, consolidation and bearing of slurry after entering the subsequent space, this paper has reviewed and analyzed the research on diffusion law, consolidation characteristics and bearing mechanism of slurry, respectively. This article focuses on the diffusion characteristics, theoretical research and experimental system development and application of slurry, systematically elaborating on the main research methods and means of research of slurry diffusion laws. It summarizes the research progress of slurry consolidation properties from three aspects: the theory of slurry consolidation, consolidation mechanism of slurry-rock interface (SRI) and mechanical properties of slurry consolidation. The research on the bearing mechanism of slurry was systematically analyzed and sorted out from five aspects: optimization of material properties, mechanical properties of slurry, relationship between microstructure and mechanical properties, interaction between slurry and surrounding rock, and control of filling rock layer. Aiming at the problems and challenges in the systematic study of the diffusion-consolidation-bearing (DCB) mechanism of the slurry in the subsequent space, four key scientific problems and ten key technical problems are proposed, and the corresponding research ideas are provided. The research results lay a research foundation for the study of DCB mechanism of filling slurry in subsequent space, with a view to providing certain support for the theoretical development and engineering application of subsequent space grouting and filling mining in coal mines.
