AB  - High-speed railway switchgear has been in long-term service under complex working conditions with multiple stress couplings, which can easily induce the generation and accumulation of characteristic gases, and may further lead to serious accidents such as explosions and fires. The electrical olfactory perception technology can accurately identify and warn of early hazards by capturing the characteristic gases produced during the evolution of defects. This paper systematically reviews the research progress in this field: Firstly, it elaborates on the decomposition characteristics of gas-solid insulating media, the molecular-scale cracking mechanism, and the transmission and diffusion laws of escaping gases in high-speed railway scenarios. Secondly, the technical system of new gas-sensitive materials, multi-sensor fusion olfactory arrays, olfactory perception devices, and system integration is summarized. Furthermore, olfactory pattern recognition, multi-source information fusion diagnosis, and explosion-proof risk early-warning assessment methods for intelligent operation and maintenance are analysed. Finally, key technical challenges and future directions are discussed to support further research and engineering implementation of external defect detection for high-speed railway switchgear.
