AB  - At this stage, news broadcast digital hosts have been widely used, but due to technical reasons, many digital people have some problems, such as obvious differences in mouth synchronization accuracy, single expression of emotional sentences, multimodal instruction conflict, etc. In order to alleviate and even solve this dilemma, this paper proposes a new real-time algorithm based on multimodal large model, hoping to effectively solve the problems of digital human. The core principle of the optimization algorithm is to alleviate multimodal conflicts by generating structured story plots. In addition, in terms of framework, the optimization algorithm uses a spatio-temporal diffusion framework. Its workflow is to generate low-resolution blueprint videos to obtain global semantics, and then upsample them into high-resolution videos through a top-down frame strategy to ensure the time consistency of long sequences. Experimental results demonstrate millisecond-level precision in facial-lip synchronization, significantly outperforming existing baselines in emotional expression, and effectively supporting dual-person dialogue generation.
