AB  - Diffusion models have recently shown promising results for language generation, yet extending them to multi-constraint sequence-to-sequence settings remains challenging. Personalized comment generation is a representative multi-constraint sequence-to-sequence task, where the model must condition on both user attributes and the source article to produce comments that are simultaneously relevant and personalized. To address this problem, a novel simplex-based diffusion model framework for personalized comments (named DiffuPercom) is proposed. Specifically, the denoising network adopts a Transformer encoder–decoder structure. By separately encoding personalized information and article content, the proposed PFA (Personalized Fusion Attention) module is used to integrate the two. The PFA module can effectively integrate personalized attribute information through weighting and masking mechanisms, thus enhancing the expression of personalized information. In addition, the current lack of publicly available datasets for personalized comment tasks hinders the progress of personalized comment generation tasks. Therefore, a personalized attribute comment dataset (named PersonalComment) is proposed, which assigns sentiment labels to each comment and can serve as a foundation for subsequent research. Finally, extensive experiments on the PersonalComment dataset have demonstrated that DiffuPercom achieves substantial improvements in diversity and attribute control, with increases of 8% and 1.7% respectively, outperforming current personalized models. In addition, in the manual evaluation, the controllability of DiffuPercom’s attributes as well as the p-value for the significant test compared to the baseline model are both less than 0.05. Furthermore, personalized comment with sentiment tendencies using classifier guidance is explored.
